course: dictionary
lesson: 1637
title: Childcare and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Childcare means looking after children, especially while their parents are at work. The word is made of two parts you already know: child and care. Care means looking after someone with kindness and attention.
explain: The word can also mean the places and services that do this job, such as nurseries, childminders, day care centres and after-school clubs. «Single parents often rely on family, friends and neighbours to help with childcare.» The sentence tells you who helps: family, friends and neighbours.
explain: Read the words around childcare to be sure which meaning fits. Childcare costs means the money paid for looking after children. Free childcare means care that parents do not have to pay for. A childcare worker is a person whose job is looking after children.
fact: Childcare means looking after children, especially while their parents are at work.
fact: Childcare can also mean the places and services that look after children, such as nurseries and after-school clubs.
fact: «Childcare costs» means the money parents pay for looking after their children.
fact: «Free childcare» means care that does not cost parents money.
fact: Childcare is an uncountable noun, so we say «some childcare», not «a childcare».
exercise: «Single parents often rely on family, friends and neighbours to help with childcare.» What does childcare mean here? | Cleaning the house before bedtime | Building new schools for children | *Looking after children while their parents are at work | Teaching children to cook and clean
exercise: Ella's mum says childcare costs are going up. What do childcare costs mean? | *The money paid for looking after children | The cost of buying new toys for children | The price of a family holiday | The weight of a child's school bag
exercise: Which of these is a place that offers childcare? | A bakery | A library | *A nursery | A bus stop
test: Childcare is an uncountable noun. Which sentence is correct? | We need three childcare for the holidays. | We need a childcares for the holidays. | We need many childcare for the holidays. | *We need some childcare for the holidays.
test: What is a childminder? | A person who builds nurseries | A teacher who works in a big school | A person who minds a stranger's car | *A person who looks after children, often in their own home
exam: In the news, a government says it will give free childcare hours. What does free childcare mean? | Nurseries will charge more money | *Parents do not have to pay for the care of their children | Schools will be closed for the summer | Children must stay at home all day
